# PART 3 — ENVIRONMENT ARCHITECTURE

## 3.1 Test and Live separation

Stripe and PayPal must have separate test and live configurations.

Never use the same credential record for both environments.

Each environment must independently store:

- Encrypted credentials.
- Provider account identifiers.
- Webhook configuration.
- Activation status.
- Connection status.
- Supported capabilities.
- Audit history.

A test-mode transaction must never be processed through live credentials.

A live-mode transaction must never be processed through test credentials.

## 3.2 Live activation

Only Super Admin can activate a live gateway.

Before activation:

- Credentials must be validated.
- Merchant eligibility must be confirmed.
- Webhook configuration must be verified.
- Provider capabilities must be verified.
- Required sandbox tests must pass.
- A live activation confirmation must be completed.

Use an explicit confirmation screen that explains the consequences.

Test Gateway must be permanently blocked from live activation.

## 3.3 Environment isolation

Every payment, refund, transaction, webhook and reconciliation record must include the correct environment.

Test and live reporting must be separated.

Test payments must not:

- Increase live revenue.
- Trigger live fulfillment.
- Deduct live inventory.
- Create real refunds.
- Affect real customer payment history.

Use explicit test-mode safeguards throughout the application, not only in the dashboard.

