# PART 8 — WEBHOOK MANAGEMENT

Every external provider must have its own webhook handler.

Requirements:

- Verify provider signatures.
- Verify timestamps where supported.
- Use raw request bodies for signature validation where required.
- Reject invalid signatures.
- Deduplicate provider event IDs.
- Prevent replay attacks.
- Store sanitized event records.
- Process events idempotently.
- Handle out-of-order events.
- Log failures.
- Support safe replay of eligible failed events.

Required event categories:

- Payment succeeded.
- Payment failed.
- Payment pending.
- Payment cancelled.
- Refund succeeded.
- Refund failed.
- Refund pending.
- Refund updated.

Use actual provider event types and documented signature requirements.

Do not fabricate Stripe or PayPal webhook event formats.

