# PART 9 — BANK TRANSFER AND COD

## 9.1 Bank Transfer

Bank Transfer is an offline/manual settlement method, not an automatic card gateway.

Customer workflow:

1. Select Bank Transfer.
2. Create a pending order/payment.
3. Display bank details and payment reference.
4. Customer submits payment proof or reference.
5. Authorized Super Admin verifies settlement.
6. Payment becomes paid.
7. Inventory/order workflow continues exactly once.

Payment proof submission must not automatically establish payment success.

Keep verification history.

## 9.2 Cash on Delivery

COD is an operational payment method.

Customer workflow:

1. Select COD.
2. Validate COD availability for address and shipping method.
3. Create the order with pending COD collection.
4. Dispatch order.
5. Record collection confirmation.
6. Mark payment paid only after authorized collection confirmation.

Support failed delivery and uncollected COD orders.

Do not treat COD order creation as payment collection.

