# PART 10 — SECURITY AND PERMISSIONS

## 10.1 Access control

Only Super Admin can:

- Add or edit gateway credentials.
- Connect or disconnect providers.
- Test credentials.
- Activate or deactivate gateways.
- Switch live mode.
- Configure webhooks.
- Run sensitive reconciliation actions.
- Perform manual settlement verification.
- Retry eligible refunds.

Other users must not access gateway configuration endpoints.

Enforce authorization in Laravel middleware and controllers, not only by hiding dashboard navigation.

## 10.2 Credential security

- Use Laravel encrypted storage.
- Never expose secrets in API responses.
- Never put secret keys in frontend localStorage.
- Never log plaintext credentials.
- Mask credential values in the UI.
- Support credential rotation.
- Separate test and live credentials.
- Prevent credentials from appearing in exceptions.
- Do not store provider secrets in source code or committed environment files.

## 10.3 Live payment safeguards

- Test Gateway cannot operate in production.
- Test credentials cannot process live payments.
- Live credentials cannot process sandbox transactions.
- Require Super Admin confirmation before activation.
- Prevent deactivation while unresolved financial operations need the gateway, unless a safe migration procedure exists.
- Preserve historical transaction access after disconnection.

